{"teams":[{"idTeam":"152989","idESPN":"0","idAPIfootball":"4467","intLoved":null,"strTeam":"Eastern District","strTeamAlternate":"Eastern District Sports Association, 東區體育會","strTeamShort":"","intFormedYear":"2002","strSport":"Soccer","strLeague":"Hong-Kong Premier League","idLeague":"4825","strLeague2":"Hong Kong FA Cup","idLeague2":"5948","strLeague3":"Hong Kong Senior Shield","idLeague3":"5947","strLeague4":"","idLeague4":null,"strLeague5":"","idLeague5":null,"strLeague6":"","idLeague6":null,"strLeague7":"","idLeague7":null,"strDivision":null,"idVenue":"20083","strStadium":"Siu Sai Wan Sports Ground","strKeywords":"","strRSS":"","strLocation":"Hong Kong","strWebsite":"","strFacebook":"","strTwitter":"","strInstagram":"","strDescriptionEN":"Eastern District Sports Association (Chinese: 東區體育會), also known as Eastern District (Chinese: 東區足球隊), is a Hong Kong professional football club which currently competes in the Hong Kong Premier League.\r\n\r\nThe team play their home matches at Siu Sai Wan Sports Ground.\r\n\r\nIn the 2002–03 season, the Hong Kong Football Association reformed the Hong Kong Second Division League and the Hong Kong Third Division League. The association suggested that different district councils form a football team based in their districts. The Eastern District Council therefore formed a football team, while the team started competing in the Hong Kong Third District Division.\r\n\r\nIn the 2008–09 season, Eastern District placed 13th out of 15 teams in the Hong Kong Third District Division. It had only won 4 matches and lost 10 matches in the league.\r\n\r\nIn the 2009–10 season, Eastern District appointed ex-Hong Kong national football team goalkeeper Goldbert Chi Chiu as their goalkeeper trainer. Despite that, their league result was worse than the previous season. It placed 13th out of 14 teams, having only won 1 match, drawn 1 match, and lost 11 matches.\r\n\r\nEastern District was promoted into the First Division after finishing 2nd in the 2015–16 Hong Kong Second Division.\r\n\r\nOn 4 July 2025, it was announced that Eastern District had been accepted into the Hong Kong Premier League for the 2025–26 season.","strDescriptionDE":null,"strDescriptionFR":null,"strDescriptionCN":null,"strDescriptionIT":null,"strDescriptionJP":null,"strDescriptionRU":null,"strDescriptionES":null,"strDescriptionPT":null,"strDescriptionSE":null,"strDescriptionNL":null,"strDescriptionHU":null,"strDescriptionNO":null,"strDescriptionIL":null,"strDescriptionPL":null,"strColour1":"","strColour2":"","strColour3":"","strGender":"Male","strCountry":"Hong Kong","strBadge":"https://r2.thesportsdb.com/images/media/team/badge/hdaaum1756402956.png","strLogo":null,"strFanart1":null,"strFanart2":null,"strFanart3":null,"strFanart4":null,"strBanner":null,"strEquipment":null,"strYoutube":"","strLocked":"unlocked"},{"idTeam":"139855","idESPN":"0","idAPIfootball":"4451","intLoved":null,"strTeam":"Eastern SC","strTeamAlternate":"Eastern Athletic Association Football Team Limited, Eastern Sports Club, 東方體育會, Eastern Football Team, 東方足球隊, Eastern Long Lions Football Team, 東方龍獅足球隊","strTeamShort":"","intFormedYear":"1932","strSport":"Soccer","strLeague":"Hong-Kong Premier League","idLeague":"4825","strLeague2":"Hong Kong FA Cup","idLeague2":"5948","strLeague3":"Hong Kong Senior Shield","idLeague3":"5947","strLeague4":"","idLeague4":null,"strLeague5":"","idLeague5":null,"strLeague6":"","idLeague6":null,"strLeague7":"","idLeague7":null,"strDivision":null,"idVenue":"19942","strStadium":"Mong Kok Stadium","strKeywords":"","strRSS":"","strLocation":"Tseung Kwan O, Hong Kong","strWebsite":"football.easternlonglions.com","strFacebook":"www.facebook.com/EASTERNLONGLIONSBASKETBALL","strTwitter":"","strInstagram":"www.instagram.com/easternlonglionsbasketball","strDescriptionEN":"Eastern Athletic Association Football Team Limited, also known as Eastern Sports Club (Chinese: 東方體育會) is a Hong Kong professional sports club with football and basketball section